{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"hekiryuu","id":"237577351532249110","is_bot":0,"username":"hekiryuu"},"author_id":"237577351532249110","channel_id":"880417697018548274","content":"```Any players that were brought to unconsciousness, will wake in a large cage in the basement with 1hp.  Inform them they have gained one level of Hampstead Damnation, but do not know what it is from (They were brought so close to the brink of death that magic was used to bring them back).  Their minds feel as if filled with cotton.  They will see all of their gear (clothes and all) in piles along one of the walls.  Around the cage is a circle made of fiendish runes (if players can read fiendish, let them know that it's somewhat fuzzy, but it seems to talk about Arbeyach, and infestation of the hive.)  The entire cage is brightly lit, to a point no one in it casts a shadow on any surface.\n\nIn this 8 foot tall room they will also see 10 cultists chanting in a large circle surrounding the cage.  While chanting, the players must make a DC10+spell’s level concentration check with disadvantage to cast spells, otherwise the spell slot is used, but instead the magic from the spell goes into the runes making them glow brighter (record spell levels that are absorbed, treating cantrips as 1/2).  As long as at least one cultist still chants, this effect stays in place, and if all 10 cultists stop chanting, the runes will explode.  Everyone in the room will have to make a DC 14 Cha save.  On a failure, they will take one level of Hampstead Damnation for every 2 spell levels absorbed by the runes.  In addition, they will be charmed by the cultists and minions (charm ends after 1 week, or if they are attacked by any of the entities that they are charmed by).\n```\nThis was also the day the tax in hammy was: \n\n```The Tax On Hampstead's Magic Today: Spell save DC’s are reduced to 10 and cannot be raised above 10.```","created_at":"2021-08-26T18:50:25.190000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"880524605008273458","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
